{#-
  The list of sleep problems on Home (SPEC §7.2, §8.1; HANDOFF §6.3; boards
  Problems-A.dc.html and Problems-Phone.dc.html, with the changes in SPEC
  §7.5): the problems by area, and only by area, one group per area
  (data/areas.csv, in its order). Each group is a plain heading with the
  area's name, description and a count, over the list of its problems.

    {% from "partials/problem-list.njk" import problemList %}
    {{ problemList(collections.problems | groupByArea(areas), keywords) }}

  Arguments:
    areas     the `collections.problems | groupByArea(areas)` list
    keywords  the rows of data/keywords.csv (SPEC §8.2), or nothing while
              the file doesn't exist. A problem's row is written to its list
              item's data-keywords, where problems.js reads it for the
              filter

  Without JavaScript (SPEC §2, §11) every area is open, so the problem
  links are always reachable. src/js/problems.js turns each area heading's
  <span> into a <button aria-expanded aria-controls> and closes the areas.
  Hooks for it are data-* attributes; classes are for styling only.

  The area headings are <h3>: the list sits under Home's <h2> "What's
  keeping you up?". Each group's id is its area_id, so /#core links to an
  area (SPEC §7.2).
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}

{#- A problem's keywords from data/keywords.csv, or nothing. -#}
{%- macro keywordsFor(slug, keywords) -%}
{%- for row in keywords -%}{%- if row.page_id == slug -%}{{ row.keywords }}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A link to a problem: short title, first-person line and an arrow, the
    same on every card (no "New" pill, SPEC §7.5). Built on .topic-card
    (components.css). The spaces between the spans keep the link's
    accessible name readable ("Tired but wired I'm tired, ..."). -#}
{%- macro topicCard(p) -%}
<a class="topic-card topic-card--row" href="{{ p.url }}">
  <span class="topic-card__text">
    <span class="topic-card__title" data-topic-title>{{ p.title }}</span>
    <span class="topic-card__statement" data-topic-statement>{{ p.statement }}</span>
  </span>
  {{ icon('arrow-right', 20, 'topic-card__arrow') }}
</a>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro problemList(areas, keywords) -%}
<div class="problems" data-problems>
  <div class="group-list">
    {%- for area in areas %}{% set n = area.problems.length %}
    <section class="group-list__group" id="{{ area.area_id }}">
      <h3 class="group-list__heading">
        <span class="group-list__header" data-group-header>
          <span class="group-list__text">
            <span class="group-list__name" data-group-name>{{ area.name }}</span>
            <span class="group-list__description">{{ area.description }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="group-list__count"><span data-group-count data-total="{{ n }}">{{ n }}</span><span class="group-list__count-unit"> {{ 'topic' if n == 1 else 'topics' }}</span></span>
          <span class="group-list__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon('chevron-down', 18) }}</span>
        </span>
      </h3>
      <ul class="group-list__problems" id="area-{{ area.area_id }}-problems" role="list" data-group-list>
        {%- for p in area.problems %}{% set kw = keywordsFor(p.slug, keywords) | trim %}
        <li data-slug="{{ p.slug }}"{% if kw | length %} data-keywords="{{ kw }}"{% endif %}>{{ topicCard(p) }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
